    "result_text": "The build passed with the acceptance test that covers exactly this scenario (`coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity`). \n\nThe change is complete. I added a conflict check to `addOwner` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n```java\nif (countOwnersInCity(owner.getCity()) >= 50) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);\n}\n```\n\nIt reuses the existing `countOwnersInCity` helper (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed city matching) that the customer-code generation already relies on, so when a city already contains 50 or more owners a create request returns **409 Conflict**. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, including the `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` acceptance test which fills a city to 50 and expects the 51st create to be rejected).",
